\pard\qc\b\f1\fs32 MQTT Implementation Documentation\par
\pard\qc\b0\f0\fs24 Scholarship Tracking System\par
\pard\qc June 2026\par
\par
\pard\b 1. Introduction\par
\b0
The Scholarship Tracking System now includes MQTT to support real-time announcement processing. MQTT is used as a lightweight messaging protocol between the announcement creation process and the announcement dispatch process.\par
\par
\pard\b 2. Purpose of MQTT in the System\par
\b0
The main purpose of MQTT is to allow the system to publish an event whenever a new announcement is added. Once the event is received, the backend can process and dispatch the announcement automatically. This improves the speed of announcement delivery and supports real-time communication inside the system.\par
\par
\pard\b 3. Where MQTT is Used\par
\b0
MQTT is implemented in the backend of the Scholarship Tracking System. It is mainly used in the announcement module.\par
\par
The following files are part of the implementation:\par
- `backend/src/services/mqttClient.js` for MQTT connection, publish, and subscribe logic.\par
- `backend/src/server.js` for starting the MQTT client during backend startup.\par
- `backend/src/controllers/announcementAdmin.controller.js` for publishing MQTT events when an admin creates an announcement.\par
- `backend/src/services/gmailAnnouncements.js` for publishing MQTT events when an announcement is ingested from Gmail.\par
- `database/migrations/002_announcement_dispatch.sql` for the `mqtt_logs` table structure.\par
\par
\pard\b 4. MQTT Workflow\par
\b0
The MQTT flow in the system works as follows:\par
1. An announcement is created by the admin or ingested from Gmail.\par
2. The backend saves the announcement in the database.\par
3. The backend publishes an MQTT message to the topic `scholarship_system/announcements/ingested`.\par
4. The backend subscriber receives the same message from the broker.\par
5. The system reads the announcement ID from the payload.\par
6. The dispatch process starts and sends the announcement to the intended users.\par
\par
\pard\b 5. MQTT Message Format\par
\b0
The published MQTT message uses JSON format.\par
\par
Example payload:\par
{\f1
{\pard\li720 announcementId: 15\par}
{\pard\li720 source: "admin"\par}
{\pard\li720 ts: "2026-06-02T09:30:00.000Z"\par}
}\f0
\par
\pard\b 6. MQTT Topic Used\par
\b0
The current topic used by the system is:\par
`scholarship_system/announcements/ingested`\par
\par
This topic is built from the environment variable `MQTT_TOPIC_BASE` plus `/announcements/ingested`.\par
\par
\pard\b 7. MQTT Configuration\par
\b0
To enable MQTT, the backend uses environment variables. The important settings are:\par
- `MQTT_ENABLED=true`\par
- `MQTT_HOST=127.0.0.1`\par
- `MQTT_PORT=1883`\par
- `MQTT_TOPIC_BASE=scholarship_system`\par
\par
Optional settings:\par
- `MQTT_URL`\par
- `MQTT_USERNAME`\par
- `MQTT_PASSWORD`\par
- `MQTT_CLIENT_ID`\par
\par
\pard\b 8. Database Support\par
\b0
The system includes an `mqtt_logs` table to store MQTT-related event records. This table keeps the announcement ID, event type, payload data, and creation timestamp. It helps monitor MQTT activity inside the system.\par
\par
\pard\b 9. Benefits of the MQTT Implementation\par
\b0
The MQTT integration provides the following benefits:\par
- Faster announcement event handling.\par
- Better support for real-time processing.\par
- Clear separation between announcement creation and dispatch.\par
- Easier integration with other services in the future.\par
- Better monitoring through stored MQTT logs.\par
\par
\pard\b 10. Conclusion\par
\b0
The MQTT implementation improves the Scholarship Tracking System by adding a real-time event-driven process for announcements. It makes the system more responsive, organized, and ready for future integrations while keeping the backend workflow simple.\par
